-- title:
--   Ordinarity contradicts decomposition-irreducibility of a second eigensystem
-- statement:
--   Fix $N\ge 1$, a finite set $S$ of natural numbers, and a complete discrete valuation domain $\mathcal{O}$, and let $\theta$ be a ring homomorphism from $\mathrm{heckeAlgebra}\,N\,2\,S$ — the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb{C}}$ of weight-two cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(N)$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S$, together with $U_q$ for primes $q\mid N$, $q\notin S$ — to the residue field of $\mathcal{O}$. Let $T$ be a complete local Noetherian $\mathcal{O}$-algebra, finite and free as an $\mathcal{O}$-module, with local structure map, and let $H$ be a Hecke–Galois datum for $(\theta,T)$: a ring homomorphism $\pi$ from the Hecke algebra to $T$ reducing to $\theta$ along the residue map, generating $T$ as an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra, such that every $\mathcal{O}$-valued lift of $\theta$ factors through $\pi$ via an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra map $T\to\mathcal{O}$, with surjective composite $\mathcal{O}\to T\to T/\mathfrak{m}_T$, together with a rank-two adically continuous representation $H.\rho$ of $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ over $T$ whose Frobenius characteristic polynomials at primes $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S$ are $X^2-\pi(T_\ell)X+\ell$ and whose residual representation is absolutely irreducible. Assume further: $p$ is a prime such that the residual representation of $H.\rho$, viewed as an adic representation over the residue field of $T$, is ordinary at $p$, i.e. for every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a non-unit of $P$ there is a submodule which is the span of a member of some basis, stable under the decomposition subgroup of $P$, and modulo which the inertia subgroup acts trivially; $\mathcal{O}'$ is a local commutative ring, $e$ a ring homomorphism between the residue fields of $\mathcal{O}$ and $\mathcal{O}'$, and $\chi$ an $\mathcal{O}'$-valued homomorphism on the Hecke algebra whose reduction is $e\circ\theta$; $\rho$ is a rank-two adically continuous Galois representation over $\mathcal{O}'$ whose characteristic polynomial at any Frobenius element for any valuation subring above a prime $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S$, equals $X^2-\chi(T_\ell)X+\ell$; and for every valuation subring above $p$, every subspace of the residual space of $\rho$ stable under the decomposition subgroup is zero or everything. The conclusion is that these hypotheses are contradictory.
--
--   This is the incompatibility, at a prime $p$, between ordinarity of a residual modular representation and the absence of a decomposition-stable line in a second representation carrying the same Hecke eigensystem; in the textbook account it is the observation that an ordinary representation is reducible on a decomposition group at $p$. It is used in the construction of points of the Hecke-algebra datum with prescribed local behaviour, via [`CuspForm.HeckeGaloisRepDatum.exists_pi_eq_and_isOrdinaryAt_of_primeFactors_subset`](thm.html#CuspForm.HeckeGaloisRepDatum.exists_pi_eq_and_isOrdinaryAt_of_primeFactors_subset).
